01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
The Italian Job is a 2003 American heist action film directed by F.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Gary Gray and screenplay by Donna Powers and Wayne Powers.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
The film stars an ensemble cast consisting of Mark Wahlberg, Charlize Theron, Edward
Norton, Jason Statham, Seth Green, Mos Def, and Donald Sutherland.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
Inspired by the 1969 British film, but with an original story, the plot follows a motley crew of
thieves who plan to steal gold from a former associate who double-crossed them.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
Despite the shared title, the plot and characters of this film differ from its source material; Gray described the film as "an homage to the original."
Most of the
film was shot on location in Venice and Los Angeles, where canals and streets, respectively, were temporarily shut down during principal photography.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
Distributed by Paramount Pictures, The Italian Job was theatrically released in the
United States on May 30, 2003, and grossed over $176 million worldwide.

18
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
Critical response was generally positive, with publications comparing it favorably to the original
film while highlighting the action sequences, performances of the cast and humor.

19
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
A sequel, The Brazilian Job, was reportedly in development
in 2004, but was subsequently cancelled.

20
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
The film explores themes of gold, california, helicopter, hacker, venice, italy.

21
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:06,000
The tone is intense.
